IMPORT prelude

-- Civil Procedure Act 2005 (NSW) -- Part 10, representative proceedings (class actions) in the Supreme Court, ss 155-184,
-- from the seat of the person with a claim in a class action.
--
-- SEAT: the individual whose claim is carried in representative proceedings: a group member (or sub-group member), and
-- the group member who starts the proceedings and becomes the representative party. Every exported question is one that
-- person would ask: "Can our claims be brought as a class action?", "Am I in the group without agreeing to it?", "By when
-- must I opt out?", "Will the judgment bind me?", "Can I be made to pay costs?", "Is my time limit still running?", "By
-- when must I claim from the fund?", "Can I appeal if the representative party does not?". The Court and the defendant
-- get no seat: what the Court must or may do is encoded as what it means for the group member.
--
-- Provisions: ss 155 (definitions), 157-158 (commencement, standing), 159 (consent), 160 (legal incapacity), 162 (opting
-- out), 163 (later causes of action), 164-167 (ending the class action and what follows), 168-169 and 181 (individual
-- questions and costs), 171 (adequacy of representation), 172 (stay of execution), 173 and 175(4) (settlement), 174
-- (representative party's own settlement and withdrawal), 175-176 (notices), 177(3) (aggregate damages), 178 (the
-- distribution fund), 179 (effect of judgment), 180(3) (appeal by another group member), 182 (suspension of limitation
-- periods), 184 (reimbursement of the representative party). Out, with reasons in NOTES.md: s 156 (application to
-- proceedings commenced after the Part commenced: transitional), s 161 (contents of the originating process: drafting
-- for the representative party's lawyers), ss 168(1), 170, 177(1)-(2),(4), 183 (open powers to give directions and make
-- orders: nothing a person can be told in advance), s 180(1),(2),(4)-(6) (form of appeals), s 178 note (the registrar's
-- 2.5% deduction under s 18A, Part 2).
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no question answers JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no (a "means" definition, a
-- condition introduced by "if", "where", "unless" or "except", a flat "must not"/"may not", a period fixed in the Act's
-- own words), or NOTHING where the Act does not answer on the facts given; each NOTHING carries a "NOTHING-kind" comment.
-- A judgment the Act leaves to the Court ("appears to the Court", "satisfied", "just", "interests of justice") is asked
-- as an input and the answer is conditional on it; it is never decided here.
--
-- Dates use only the prelude's built-in DATE functions (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL), not daydate.
--
-- Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website (as collected by the Open Australian Legal Corpus on
-- 10 March 2025; corpus document dated 1 July 2024; unofficial, possibly out of date). CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING.
-- Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Civil Procedure Act 2005, Part 10 -- representative proceedings`

§§ `The nouns`

-- s 155: the persons the Part names. "group member" means a member of the group on whose behalf the proceedings were
-- commenced; "representative party" means the person who commenced them; "sub-group member" and "sub-group
-- representative party" are those of a sub-group established under s 168.
DECLARE `My part in the class action` IS ONE OF
    `a group member`
    `a sub-group member`
    `the representative party`
    `a sub-group representative party`

-- s 159(2): the persons who are group members only if they consent in writing.
DECLARE `What kind of person I am` IS ONE OF
    `an individual, company or other person not listed in section 159(2)`
    `the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory`
    `a Minister of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory`
    `a body corporate established for a public purpose by law, other than an incorporated company or association`
    `an officer of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory, acting in that capacity`

-- s 162(2): the answer to "have I opted out?".
DECLARE `My opt-out` IS ONE OF
    `I have opted out in time`
    `my notice was not given before the date fixed, so it does not opt me out`
    `only a written notice given under the local rules opts me out`

-- ss 164-166: the ground on which the Court is satisfied under s 166(1), with s 166(2).
DECLARE `Section 166 ground` IS ONE OF
    `no section 166 ground`
    `continuing as a class action is likely to cost more than separate proceedings`
    `all the relief can be obtained by other proceedings`
    `a class action will not be an efficient and effective way to deal with the claims`
    `the representative party cannot adequately represent the group members`
    `it is otherwise inappropriate to pursue the claims by a class action`
    `only that the group does not include everyone, or was put together for a litigation funding arrangement`

-- s 167: what follows an order that the proceedings no longer continue under the Part.
DECLARE `After the class action ends` IS ONE OF
    `I may continue the proceedings on my own behalf against the defendant`
    `I may apply to be joined as a plaintiff, and the Court may order it`
    `section 167 does not apply: no order under section 164, 165 or 166 has been made`

-- s 181 with ss 168, 169: what costs can be awarded against me.
DECLARE `My exposure to costs` IS ONE OF
    `no costs can be awarded against me`
    `only the costs of determining my individual question`
    `section 181 does not protect the representative party: the ordinary costs rules apply`

-- s 175: the matters notice of which group members must or may be given.
DECLARE `Matter for notice` IS ONE OF
    `the start of the class action and my right to opt out by the date fixed`
    `the defendant's application to dismiss for want of prosecution`
    `the representative party's application for leave to withdraw`
    `money brought into Court in answer to a cause of action in the class action`
    `any other matter`

-- s 178(3)(c), (4): the answer to "is my claim on the fund in time?".
DECLARE `My fund claim` IS ONE OF
    `my claim is in time`
    `my claim is late, but the Court may allow it if it is just to do so`
    `my claim is late and the Court cannot allow it, because the fund has been fully distributed or applied`

-- s 180(3): the answer to "can I appeal for the group?".
DECLARE `My appeal for the group` IS ONE OF
    `I may bring the appeal as representing the group or sub-group`
    `the further 21 days have passed`
    `not yet: the representative party's own time to appeal has not run out`
    `section 180(3) does not apply: the representative party appealed in time`
    `section 180(3) does not apply: it is for another member, not the representative party`

-- s 182: the state of my own limitation period.
DECLARE `My limitation period` IS ONE OF
    `the class action does not affect it: it had already expired when the class action started`
    `it is suspended while the class action runs`
    `it is running again`

-- The parties and acts of the three regulative rules (ss 162(2), 178(3)(c), 180(3)).
DECLARE `Class action party` IS ONE OF `the group member`
DECLARE `Class action act` IS ONE OF
    `give written notice of opting out under the local rules`
    `make a claim for payment out of the fund`
    `bring an appeal as representing the group`

§§ `Dates`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is before` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` `plus days` `days` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day` PLUS `days`)

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days in the month of` `the day` MEANS
    DATE_SERIAL `the first of the next month` MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (DATE_MONTH `the day`) (DATE_YEAR `the day`))
    WHERE
        `the first of the next month` MEANS
            IF DATE_MONTH `the day` EQUALS 12
            THEN DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 (DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS 1)
            ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (DATE_MONTH `the day` PLUS 1) (DATE_YEAR `the day`)

-- READING (fork F9): "6 months ... after the day" ends on the same day of the month six months later, or on that
-- month's last day where it is shorter (31 August to 28 or 29 February). The Interpretation Act 1987 is not deposited.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`six months after` `the day` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY `the smaller day` `the month` `the year`
    WHERE
        `months from year zero` MEANS (DATE_YEAR `the day`) TIMES 12 PLUS (DATE_MONTH `the day` MINUS 1) PLUS 6
        `the year` MEANS FLOOR (`months from year zero` DIVIDED BY 12)
        `the month` MEANS `months from year zero` MINUS (`the year` TIMES 12) PLUS 1
        `the smaller day` MEANS
            IF DATE_DAY `the day` AT MOST `the number of days in the month of` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 `the month` `the year`)
            THEN DATE_DAY `the day`
            ELSE `the number of days in the month of` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 `the month` `the year`)

§§ `ss 157, 158 -- starting a class action`

-- s 157(1) "Subject to this Part, where-- (a) 7 or more persons have claims against the same person, and (b) the claims
-- of all those persons are in respect of, or arise out of, the same, similar or related circumstances, and (c) the
-- claims of all those persons give rise to a substantial common question of law or fact, proceedings may be commenced by
-- one or more of those persons as representing some or all of them." s 158(1): a person has sufficient interest if the
-- person has standing to sue the other person on the person's own behalf. A "where" condition: when it fails, JUST
-- FALSE. s 157(2): the kind of relief (equitable, damages, damages needing individual assessment, different for each)
-- and separate contracts or acts do not matter, so they are not asked. Whether the common question is "substantial" is
-- for the Court: asked as an input.
@export Can I start a class action (representative proceedings) in the NSW Supreme Court for myself and others with claims against the same person (ss 157, 158)?
GIVEN `the number of persons with claims against the same person` IS A NUMBER @desc How many persons, counting yourself, have claims against the same person (the defendant)
      `I have a claim against that person myself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you yourself have a claim against that person that you could bring in your own name (s 158(1) standing)
      `the claims arise out of the same, similar or related circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether all those claims are in respect of, or arise out of, the same, similar or related circumstances
      `the claims give rise to a substantial common question of law or fact` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether all those claims raise a substantial question of law or fact in common (the Court decides; answer as you expect it to)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I start a class action` MEANS
    IF     `the number of persons with claims against the same person` AT LEAST 7
       AND `I have a claim against that person myself`
       AND `the claims arise out of the same, similar or related circumstances`
       AND `the claims give rise to a substantial common question of law or fact`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 159, 160 -- who is a group member`

-- s 159 "(1) ... the consent of a person to be a group member is not required. (2) None of the following is a group
-- member in representative proceedings unless the person gives consent in writing to being so-- ...". s 155 "group
-- member means a member of a group of persons on whose behalf representative proceedings have been commenced": a "means"
-- definition, so a person outside the group described is not one (JUST FALSE). An "unless" once met: JUST TRUE (fork F2).
@export Am I a group member in this class action, even though I was not asked to agree (ss 155, 159)?
GIVEN `I fall within the description of the group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you fall within the group of persons on whose behalf the class action was started, as the originating process describes it
      `what kind of person I am` IS A `What kind of person I am` @desc What kind of person you are. One of: "an individual, company or other person not listed in section 159(2)", "the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory", "a Minister of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory", "a body corporate established for a public purpose by law, other than an incorporated company or association", "an officer of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory, acting in that capacity"
      `I have consented in writing to be a group member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given written consent to be a group member
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I a group member` MEANS
    IF (NOT `I fall within the description of the group`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `what kind of person I am` EQUALS `an individual, company or other person not listed in section 159(2)`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE IF `I have consented in writing to be a group member`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 160(1) "It is not necessary for a person under legal incapacity to have a tutor merely in order to be a group
-- member." A flat negative: JUST FALSE. For a person not under legal incapacity the section says nothing (NOTHING).
@export Do I need a tutor just to be a group member, if I am under a legal incapacity (s 160(1))?
GIVEN `I am under a legal incapacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a person under legal incapacity (for example a child, or a person who cannot manage their own affairs)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Do I need a tutor to be a group member` MEANS
    IF `I am under a legal incapacity`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (the text is silent: s 160 speaks only of persons under legal incapacity)

-- s 160(2) "A group member who is a person under legal incapacity may only take a step in representative proceedings, or
-- conduct part of the proceedings, by the member's tutor." A list closed by "only": JUST FALSE for a step taken other
-- than by the tutor; for a group member not under incapacity, NOTHING.
@export Can I take a step in the class action myself, rather than through my tutor (s 160(2))?
GIVEN `I am under a legal incapacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a person under legal incapacity (for example a child, or a person who cannot manage their own affairs)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I take a step without my tutor` MEANS
    IF `I am under a legal incapacity`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (the text is silent: s 160(2) speaks only of a group member under legal incapacity)

§§ `s 162 -- opting out`

-- s 162(1) "The Court must fix a date before which a group member may opt out" and (2) "A group member may opt out ... by
-- written notice given under the local rules before the date so fixed." (3) The date may be extended: the latest date
-- fixed is the input. "before the date": the last day is the day before it (fork F3).
@export What is the last day on which I can give my written notice opting out of the class action (s 162)?
GIVEN `the date fixed for opting out` IS A DATE @desc The date the Court has fixed before which group members may opt out (the latest one, if the Court has extended it under s 162(3))
GIVETH A DATE
`The last day to opt out` MEANS `the date fixed for opting out` `plus days` (0 MINUS 1)

-- The opt-out as a rule. Jurally opting out is a power, not a duty; the rule models the period as a MUST with LEST BREACH
-- so that a notice given too late is told apart from one in time. Time is the day number (DATE_SERIAL); time 0 is long
-- before any class action.
GIVEN `the last day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Class action party` `Class action act`
`s 162(2) -- a group member who wants to opt out must give written notice before the date fixed` `the last day` MEANS
    PARTY `the group member`
    MUST `give written notice of opting out under the local rules`
    WITHIN `the last day`
    LEST BREACH BY `the group member` BECAUSE "opt-out notice not given before the date fixed under s 162(1) (s 162(2))"

@export Have I opted out of the class action in time (s 162)?
GIVEN `the date fixed for opting out` IS A DATE @desc The date the Court has fixed before which group members may opt out (the latest one, if the Court has extended it under s 162(3))
      `I gave a written notice under the local rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your opt-out was a written notice given in the way the Supreme Court's rules require
      `the day I gave my notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave your opt-out notice
GIVETH A `My opt-out`
`Have I opted out in time` MEANS
    IF (NOT `I gave a written notice under the local rules`)
    THEN `only a written notice given under the local rules opts me out`
    ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`s 162(2) -- a group member who wants to opt out must give written notice before the date fixed` `the last day`) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the day given`), (EVENT `the group member` `give written notice of opting out under the local rules` `the day given`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `I have opted out in time`
         OTHERWISE `my notice was not given before the date fixed, so it does not opt me out`
    WHERE
        `the last day` MEANS DATE_SERIAL (`The last day to opt out` `the date fixed for opting out`)
        `the day given` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the day I gave my notice`

-- s 162(4) "Except with the leave of the Court, the hearing of representative proceedings must not commence earlier than
-- the date before which a group member may opt out of the proceedings." A flat negative with "except": JUST FALSE before
-- the date without leave; otherwise the section is no bar, JUST TRUE (fork F4).
@export Can the hearing of the class action start on that day, given my opt-out date (s 162(4))?
GIVEN `the date fixed for opting out` IS A DATE @desc The date the Court has fixed before which group members may opt out (the latest one, if extended)
      `the day the hearing is to start` IS A DATE @desc The day the hearing of the class action is listed to start
      `the Court has given leave to start earlier` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has given leave for the hearing to start before that date
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the hearing start then` MEANS
    IF     `the day the hearing is to start` `is before` `the date fixed for opting out`
       AND (NOT `the Court has given leave to start earlier`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 163 -- a cause of action that accrued after the class action started`

-- s 163(1) the Court may, on the representative party's application, give leave to amend the group description; (2) it
-- "may be altered so as to include a person-- (a) whose cause of action accrued after the commencement ... but before
-- such date as the Court fixes when giving leave, and (b) who would have been included in the group, or, with the
-- consent of the person would have been included in the group, if the cause of action had accrued before the
-- commencement". A grant limited in its own wording: a person outside (a) or (b) answers NOTHING. Without leave the
-- description is not altered: JUST FALSE (fork F5).
@export Can the group be widened to include me, although my cause of action arose after the class action started (s 163)?
GIVEN `the day the class action was started` IS A DATE @desc The day the class action was commenced
      `the day my cause of action accrued` IS A DATE @desc The day your own cause of action accrued (arose)
      `the date the Court fixes` IS A DATE @desc The date the Court fixes when giving leave; causes of action accruing before it can be included (any date if none is fixed yet)
      `I would have been in the group had it accrued before the start` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you would have been included in the group (or, with your consent, would have been) if your cause of action had accrued before the class action started
      `the Court gives leave on the representative party's application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court gives leave, on the representative party's application, to amend the description of the group
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the group be widened to include me` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the day the class action was started` `is before` `the day my cause of action accrued`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (a grant limited in its own wording: s 163 is for causes of action accruing after the start)
    ELSE IF (NOT `the day my cause of action accrued` `is before` `the date the Court fixes`)
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (a grant limited in its own wording: accrued on or after the date the Court fixes)
         ELSE IF (NOT `I would have been in the group had it accrued before the start`)
              THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (a grant limited in its own wording: s 163(2)(b) not met)
              ELSE IF `the Court gives leave on the representative party's application`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 164-167 -- the class action ending as a class action`

-- s 164 (fewer than 7 group members appear likely), s 165 (money relief; on the defendant's application, distribution
-- costs likely excessive against the likely total), s 166 (on the defendant's application or of the Court's own motion,
-- in the interests of justice, on a ground in (1)(a)-(e); (2) not "inappropriate" merely because the group is not
-- everyone or was aggregated for a litigation funding arrangement). Each power is introduced by "if": when none holds,
-- JUST FALSE ("these sections give no power on these facts"). Every judgment is the Court's and is asked as an input.
@export Could the Court order that our proceedings no longer continue as a class action (ss 164-166)?
GIVEN `it appears likely to the Court that there are fewer than 7 group members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it appears likely to the Court that there are fewer than 7 group members (s 164)
      `the relief claimed includes payment of money to group members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the relief claimed is or includes payment of money to group members, other than costs (s 165(a))
      `on the defendant's application the Court concludes distribution would cost too much` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the defendant's application, the Court concludes that the cost to the defendant of identifying group members and distributing to them would likely be excessive compared with the likely total (s 165(b))
      `the section 166 ground` IS A `Section 166 ground` @desc The ground, if any, on which the Court is satisfied it is in the interests of justice to stop the class action (s 166(1)). One of: "no section 166 ground", "continuing as a class action is likely to cost more than separate proceedings", "all the relief can be obtained by other proceedings", "a class action will not be an efficient and effective way to deal with the claims", "the representative party cannot adequately represent the group members", "it is otherwise inappropriate to pursue the claims by a class action", "only that the group does not include everyone, or was put together for a litigation funding arrangement"
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Could the class action be stopped` MEANS
    IF    `it appears likely to the Court that there are fewer than 7 group members`
       OR (`the relief claimed includes payment of money to group members` AND `on the defendant's application the Court concludes distribution would cost too much`)
       OR `a section 166 ground holds`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `a section 166 ground holds` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the section 166 ground`
            WHEN `no section 166 ground` THEN FALSE
            WHEN `only that the group does not include everyone, or was put together for a litigation funding arrangement` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 167(1) "If the Court makes an order under section 164, 165 or 166 that proceedings no longer continue under this
-- Part-- (a) the proceedings may be continued as proceedings by the representative party on the party's own behalf
-- against the defendant, and (b) on the application of a person who was a group member ..., the Court may order that the
-- person be joined as an applicant". A sub-group representative party is a group member, so (b) (fork F6).
@export If the class action is ordered not to continue as a class action, what can I do (s 167)?
GIVEN `my part in the class action` IS A `My part in the class action` @desc Your part in the class action. One of: "a group member", "a sub-group member", "the representative party", "a sub-group representative party"
      `the Court has ordered under section 164, 165 or 166 that it no longer continue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has ordered, under s 164, 165 or 166, that the proceedings no longer continue as a class action
GIVETH AN `After the class action ends`
`What can I do after the class action ends` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the Court has ordered under section 164, 165 or 166 that it no longer continue`)
    THEN `section 167 does not apply: no order under section 164, 165 or 166 has been made`
    ELSE IF `my part in the class action` EQUALS `the representative party`
         THEN `I may continue the proceedings on my own behalf against the defendant`
         ELSE `I may apply to be joined as a plaintiff, and the Court may order it`

§§ `ss 168, 169, 181 -- individual questions and costs`

-- s 181 "Despite section 98, in any representative proceedings, the Court may not award costs against a person on whose
-- behalf the proceedings have been commenced (other than a representative party) except as authorised by sections 168
-- and 169." s 169(2): an individual group member permitted to appear on a question relating only to that member's claim
-- "is liable for costs associated with the determination of the question". s 168 authorises no costs order in its own
-- words, so it adds nothing (fork F7). A sub-group representative party is not "a representative party" (s 155), so
-- s 181 protects it (fork F7).
@export Can the Court order me to pay costs in the class action (ss 169, 181)?
GIVEN `my part in the class action` IS A `My part in the class action` @desc Your part in the class action. One of: "a group member", "a sub-group member", "the representative party", "a sub-group representative party"
      `the Court has let me appear on a question about my claim only` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has permitted you to appear to have a question decided that relates only to your own claim (s 169(1))
GIVETH A `My exposure to costs`
`Can I be made to pay costs` MEANS
    IF `my part in the class action` EQUALS `the representative party`
    THEN `section 181 does not protect the representative party: the ordinary costs rules apply`
    ELSE IF `the Court has let me appear on a question about my claim only`
         THEN `only the costs of determining my individual question`
         ELSE `no costs can be awarded against me`

§§ `ss 171, 172 -- representation and stay`

-- s 171(1) "If, on application by a group member, it appears to the Court that a representative party is not able
-- adequately to represent the interests of the group members, the Court may substitute another group member as
-- representative party"; (2) likewise for a sub-group, "another person". An "if" condition: JUST FALSE when it fails.
@export If I apply, can the Court replace our representative party (s 171)?
GIVEN `I am a member of the group or sub-group concerned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a member of the group (or of the sub-group) that the representative party (or sub-group representative party) represents
      `it appears to the Court the representative cannot adequately represent us` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it appears to the Court that the representative party (or sub-group representative party) is not able adequately to represent the members' interests
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the Court replace our representative` MEANS
    IF `I am a member of the group or sub-group concerned` AND `it appears to the Court the representative cannot adequately represent us`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 172 "If a defendant in representative proceedings commences proceedings in the Court against a group member, the
-- Court may order a stay of execution in respect of any relief awarded to the group member in the representative
-- proceedings until the other proceedings are determined." An "if" condition; "until" fixes the period.
@export Can my award in the class action be held back because the defendant has sued me (s 172)?
GIVEN `the defendant has started proceedings against me in the Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the defendant in the class action has started proceedings against you in the Supreme Court
      `those proceedings have been determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether those other proceedings have been decided
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my award be stayed` MEANS
    IF `the defendant has started proceedings against me in the Supreme Court` AND (NOT `those proceedings have been determined`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 173, 174, 175(4) -- settlement and withdrawal`

-- s 173(1) "Representative proceedings may not be settled or discontinued without the approval of the Court." s 175(4)
-- "Unless the Court is satisfied that it is just to do so, an application for approval of a settlement under section 173
-- must not be determined unless notice has been given to group members." Flat negatives: JUST FALSE when barred.
@export Can the Court decide whether to approve the settlement of our class action now (ss 173, 175(4))?
GIVEN `notice of the settlement application has been given to group members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether group members have been given notice of the application for approval of the settlement
      `the Court is satisfied it is just to decide without that notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court is satisfied that it is just to decide the application without notice having been given
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the settlement be decided now` MEANS
    IF `notice of the settlement application has been given to group members` OR `the Court is satisfied it is just to decide without that notice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

@export Can our class action be settled or discontinued without the Court's approval (s 173(1))?
GIVEN `the Court has approved it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has approved the settlement or discontinuance
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can it be settled` MEANS
    IF `the Court has approved it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 174(4) "Before granting a person leave to withdraw as a representative party-- (a) the Court must be satisfied that
-- notice of the application has been given to group members in accordance with section 175 (1) and in sufficient time
-- for them to apply to have another person substituted ..., and (b) any application for the substitution of another
-- group member as a representative party must have been determined." Conditions on the grant: JUST FALSE when either
-- fails; when both hold, the Court may grant leave (JUST TRUE is "may", not "will").
@export Can the Court let our representative party withdraw yet (s 174)?
GIVEN `the Court is satisfied we were told in time to seek a substitute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court is satisfied that group members were given notice of the application to withdraw, under s 175(1), in enough time to apply for another person to be substituted
      `every application to substitute a representative has been decided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every application to substitute another group member as representative party has been decided (answer yes if none was made)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can our representative withdraw` MEANS
    IF `the Court is satisfied we were told in time to seek a substitute` AND `every application to substitute a representative has been decided`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 175, 176 -- notices`

-- s 175(1) notice "must be given" of (a) the start and the right to opt out, (b) a want-of-prosecution dismissal
-- application, (c) a representative party's application to withdraw; (2) the Court may dispense with any of them "if the
-- relief sought ... does not include any claim for damages"; (3) "If the Court so orders", notice of money brought into
-- Court; (5) the Court may order notice of any matter. A dispensation where damages are claimed is outside s 175(2) and
-- leaves the duty in place (fork F8).
@export Must I, as a group member, be given notice of this matter (s 175)?
GIVEN `the matter` IS A `Matter for notice` @desc The matter. One of: "the start of the class action and my right to opt out by the date fixed", "the defendant's application to dismiss for want of prosecution", "the representative party's application for leave to withdraw", "money brought into Court in answer to a cause of action in the class action", "any other matter"
      `the relief sought includes a claim for damages` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the relief sought in the class action includes any claim for damages
      `the Court has dispensed with the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has ordered that this notice need not be given
      `the Court has ordered the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has ordered that notice of this matter be given to group members
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must I be given notice` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the matter`
    WHEN `money brought into Court in answer to a cause of action in the class action` THEN
        IF `the Court has ordered the notice` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `any other matter` THEN
        IF `the Court has ordered the notice` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (the text is silent: s 175(5) is a power, unused)
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the Court has dispensed with the notice` AND (NOT `the relief sought includes a claim for damages`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 176(8) "The failure of a group member to receive or respond to a notice does not affect a step taken, an order made,
-- or a judgment given, in any proceedings." A flat negative.
@export If I did not receive, or did not answer, a notice about the class action, does that undo what was done (s 176(8))?
GIVEN `I did not receive or did not respond to a notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you failed to receive, or failed to respond to, a notice given under s 175
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does missing a notice undo anything` MEANS
    IF `I did not receive or did not respond to a notice`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (the text is silent: s 176(8) speaks only of a notice not received or not answered)

§§ `ss 177, 178, 179 -- judgment, the fund and who is bound`

-- s 177(3) "Subject to section 173, the Court is not to make an award of damages under subsection (1) (f) [an aggregate
-- amount without specifying individual amounts] unless a reasonably accurate assessment can be made of the total amount
-- to which group members will be entitled". "unless": JUST FALSE when it fails.
@export Can the Court award our damages as one aggregate sum, without fixing each member's amount (s 177)?
GIVEN `a reasonably accurate assessment of the group's total can be made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a reasonably accurate assessment can be made of the total amount group members will be entitled to under the judgment (the Court decides)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can damages be awarded in aggregate` MEANS
    IF `a reasonably accurate assessment of the group's total can be made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 178(3)(c) the order constituting a fund must "specify a day (which is 6 months or more after the day on which the
-- order is made) on or before which the group members are to make a claim for payment out of the fund". A period fixed
-- in the Act's own words: JUST FALSE when the day is earlier.
@export Does the day fixed for claims on the fund give at least the 6 months the Act requires (s 178(3)(c))?
GIVEN `the day the fund order was made` IS A DATE @desc The day the Court made the order setting up the fund
      `the day fixed for claims` IS A DATE @desc The day the order fixes, on or before which group members are to claim payment out of the fund
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does the claim day give six months` MEANS
    IF `the day fixed for claims` `is before` (`six months after` `the day the fund order was made`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- The fund claim as a rule. As with opting out, claiming is a power; the period is modelled as MUST with LEST BREACH.
GIVEN `the last day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Class action party` `Class action act`
`s 178(3)(c) -- a group member must claim from the fund on or before the day fixed` `the last day` MEANS
    PARTY `the group member`
    MUST `make a claim for payment out of the fund`
    WITHIN `the last day`
    LEST BREACH BY `the group member` BECAUSE "claim on the fund made after the day fixed under s 178(3)(c); late only with the Court's allowance (s 178(4))"

-- s 178(4) "The Court may allow a group member to make a claim after the day fixed ... if-- (a) the fund has not already
-- been fully distributed or applied in accordance with an order under subsection (5), and (b) it is just to do so."
@export Is my claim for payment out of the class action fund in time, and if not, can the Court still allow it (s 178(3), (4))?
GIVEN `the day fixed for claims` IS A DATE @desc The day fixed by the Court's order, on or before which group members are to claim payment out of the fund
      `the day I make my claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you make (or will make) your claim on the fund
      `the fund has been fully distributed or paid out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the fund has already been fully distributed, or paid out to the defendant under an order under s 178(5)
GIVETH A `My fund claim`
`Is my fund claim in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`s 178(3)(c) -- a group member must claim from the fund on or before the day fixed` (DATE_SERIAL `the day fixed for claims`)) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the claim day`), (EVENT `the group member` `make a claim for payment out of the fund` `the claim day`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN `my claim is in time`
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the fund has been fully distributed or paid out`
        THEN `my claim is late and the Court cannot allow it, because the fund has been fully distributed or applied`
        ELSE `my claim is late, but the Court may allow it if it is just to do so`
    WHERE
        `the claim day` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the day I make my claim`

-- s 179 "A judgment given in representative proceedings-- (a) must describe or otherwise identify the group members who
-- will be affected by it, and (b) binds all such persons other than any person who has opted out of the proceedings
-- under section 162." "other than": JUST FALSE for a person who opted out. A person the judgment does not identify is
-- outside s 179; whether they are bound is for the general law (NOTHING; fork F10).
@export Will the judgment in the class action bind me (s 179)?
GIVEN `the judgment identifies me as a group member affected by it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the judgment describes or otherwise identifies you among the group members affected by it
      `I opted out under section 162` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you opted out of the class action in time under s 162
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Will the judgment bind me` MEANS
    IF `I opted out under section 162`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the judgment identifies me as a group member affected by it`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the sources: a person not identified by the judgment is left to the general law)

§§ `s 180(3) -- appealing when the representative party does not`

-- s 180(3) "If the representative party or the sub-group representative party does not bring an appeal within the time
-- provided for instituting appeals, another member of the group or sub-group may, within a further 21 days, bring an
-- appeal as representing the group members or sub-group members". The time for instituting appeals is set by the rules
-- of court (not deposited): its last day is an input. The further 21 days end 21 days after that last day (fork F11).
@export What is the last day on which I could appeal for the group if the representative party does not (s 180(3))?
GIVEN `the last day of the ordinary time to appeal` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the time the rules of court allow for instituting an appeal from the judgment
GIVETH A DATE
`The last day for my appeal for the group` MEANS `the last day of the ordinary time to appeal` `plus days` 21

GIVEN `the last day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Class action party` `Class action act`
`s 180(3) -- another member may appeal for the group within a further 21 days` `the last day` MEANS
    PARTY `the group member`
    MUST `bring an appeal as representing the group`
    WITHIN `the last day`
    LEST BREACH BY `the group member` BECAUSE "appeal for the group brought after the further 21 days allowed by s 180(3)"

@export Can I bring an appeal for the group because the representative party has not appealed (s 180(3))?
GIVEN `my part in the class action` IS A `My part in the class action` @desc Your part in the class action. One of: "a group member", "a sub-group member", "the representative party", "a sub-group representative party"
      `the representative party appealed within the ordinary time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the representative party (or, for a sub-group, the sub-group representative party) brought an appeal within the time the rules of court allow
      `the last day of the ordinary time to appeal` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the time the rules of court allow for instituting an appeal from the judgment
      `the day I would bring my appeal` IS A DATE @desc The day you would file your appeal
GIVETH A `My appeal for the group`
`Can I appeal for the group` MEANS
    IF `my part in the class action` EQUALS `the representative party`
    THEN `section 180(3) does not apply: it is for another member, not the representative party`
    ELSE IF `the representative party appealed within the ordinary time`
         THEN `section 180(3) does not apply: the representative party appealed in time`
         ELSE IF (NOT `the last day of the ordinary time to appeal` `is before` `the day I would bring my appeal`)
              THEN `not yet: the representative party's own time to appeal has not run out`
              ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`s 180(3) -- another member may appeal for the group within a further 21 days` `the last day`) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the appeal day`), (EVENT `the group member` `bring an appeal as representing the group` `the appeal day`))
                   WHEN FULFILLED THEN `I may bring the appeal as representing the group or sub-group`
                   OTHERWISE `the further 21 days have passed`
    WHERE
        `the last day` MEANS DATE_SERIAL (`The last day for my appeal for the group` `the last day of the ordinary time to appeal`)
        `the appeal day` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the day I would bring my appeal`

§§ `s 182 -- my own limitation period while the class action runs`

-- s 182 "(1) On the commencement of any representative proceedings, the running of the limitation period that applies to
-- the claim of a group member ... is suspended. (2) The limitation period does not begin to run again unless either the
-- member opts out ... under section 162 or the proceedings, and any appeals ..., are determined without finally
-- disposing of the group member's claim. (3) However, nothing in this section affects ... a group member who, immediately
-- before the commencement ..., was barred by the expiration of that period". A period whose last day is the day the
-- class action started was not expired "immediately before" it (fork F12). The period resumes on the earlier of the
-- opt-out and the determination; the days left on the day it was suspended are added to the day it resumes (fork F13).
-- Situation: this group only arises for a group member who has a limitation period of their own (the Limitation Act
-- 1969 or another law sets its last day, asked as a fact).
GIVEN `my last day apart from the class action` IS A DATE
      `the day the class action was started` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `my period had expired before the class action started` IF
    `my last day apart from the class action` `is before` `the day the class action was started`

GIVEN `I opted out` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day I opted out` IS A DATE
      `it was determined without finally disposing of my claim` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day of that determination` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day my period resumed` `I opted out` `the day I opted out` `it was determined without finally disposing of my claim` `the day of that determination` MEANS
    IF `I opted out` AND `it was determined without finally disposing of my claim`
    THEN IF `the day of that determination` `is before` `the day I opted out`
         THEN `the day of that determination`
         ELSE `the day I opted out`
    ELSE IF `I opted out`
         THEN `the day I opted out`
         ELSE `the day of that determination`

@export Is the time limit for my own claim suspended by the class action (s 182)?
GIVEN `my last day apart from the class action` IS A DATE @desc The last day on which you could have started your own proceedings on the claim under the limitation period that applies to it, if there were no class action
      `the day the class action was started` IS A DATE @desc The day the class action was commenced
      `I opted out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have opted out of the class action under s 162
      `the class action was decided without finally disposing of my claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the class action, and any appeals, have been determined without finally disposing of your claim
GIVETH A `My limitation period`
`Is my limitation period suspended` MEANS
    IF `my period had expired before the class action started` `my last day apart from the class action` `the day the class action was started`
    THEN `the class action does not affect it: it had already expired when the class action started`
    ELSE IF `I opted out` OR `the class action was decided without finally disposing of my claim`
         THEN `it is running again`
         ELSE `it is suspended while the class action runs`

@export What is now the last day for starting my own proceedings on my claim, given the class action (s 182)?
GIVEN `my last day apart from the class action` IS A DATE @desc The last day on which you could have started your own proceedings on the claim under the limitation period that applies to it, if there were no class action
      `the day the class action was started` IS A DATE @desc The day the class action was commenced
      `I opted out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have opted out of the class action under s 162
      `the day I opted out` IS A DATE @desc The day your opt-out took effect (any day if you have not opted out)
      `the class action was decided without finally disposing of my claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the class action, and any appeals, have been determined without finally disposing of your claim
      `the day of that decision` IS A DATE @desc The day of that final determination (any day if there is none)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`My last day now` MEANS
    IF `my period had expired before the class action started` `my last day apart from the class action` `the day the class action was started`
    THEN JUST `my last day apart from the class action`
    ELSE IF `I opted out` OR `the class action was decided without finally disposing of my claim`
         THEN JUST ((`the day my period resumed` `I opted out` `the day I opted out` `the class action was decided without finally disposing of my claim` `the day of that decision`) `plus days` `the days left`)
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (no last day yet: the period is suspended and the text fixes no day while it is)
    WHERE
        `the days left` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `my last day apart from the class action` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the day the class action was started`

§§ `s 184 -- reimbursing the representative party out of the damages`

-- s 184(1) "If the Court has made an award of damages in representative proceedings, the representative party or a
-- sub-group representative party, or a person who has been such a party, may apply"; (2) "If ... the Court is satisfied
-- that the costs reasonably incurred ... by the person making the application are likely to exceed the costs recoverable
-- by the person from the defendant, the Court may order that an amount equal to the whole or a part of the excess be paid
-- to that person out of the damages awarded." The answer is the most the Court can order; 0 where the "if" fails. The
-- Court's estimates of the two amounts are inputs. Asked from both sides: the representative party who is paid, and the
-- group member whose damages it comes out of.
@export What is the most the Court can order paid out of the group's damages to reimburse the representative party's costs (s 184)?
GIVEN `the Court has made an award of damages` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has made an award of damages in the class action
      `the costs the representative reasonably incurred` IS A NUMBER @desc The costs, in dollars, the representative party (or sub-group representative party) reasonably incurred in the class action, as the Court is satisfied they are likely to be
      `the costs recoverable from the defendant` IS A NUMBER @desc The costs, in dollars, that party can recover from the defendant, as the Court is satisfied they are likely to be
GIVETH A NUMBER
`The most the representative can be reimbursed` MEANS
    IF `the Court has made an award of damages` AND `the costs the representative reasonably incurred` GREATER THAN `the costs recoverable from the defendant`
    THEN `the costs the representative reasonably incurred` MINUS `the costs recoverable from the defendant`
    ELSE 0
